[38;5;231m⏺[39m Using hyperpowers:using-hyperpowers — the ladder puts this at rung 1, so I'm flagging before editing.

  The change itself is one line in [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m: [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m.

  The consequence beyond that line: session lifetime is security posture. Going 30m → 8h means a stolen session token,
  an unattended logged-in browser, or a hijacked session stays valid for a full working day instead of half an hour — a
  16x widening of the window in which a compromised session can be used. [38;5;153mserver.js:2[39m confirms this value is what
  actually expires sessions, so nothing else mitigates it.

  That may well be exactly what you want (long-lived internal tool, dev convenience, reducing re-login friction). I just
  need the explicit yes before making it.

  Confirm and I'll change the value — nothing else.

